            <ArticleTitle>Adjunctive thrombolytic agents with coronary interventional techniques.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>573-84</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Thrombolytics are used in a variety of interventional procedures, including direct lytic therapy, and in conjunction with PTCA, directional atherectomy and intracoronary stenting. The dosage and variety of thrombolytics is controversial. This article examines all potential uses of thrombolytics and reports on major trials using thrombolytics in these situations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
